nism: Halving-Preserving Issuance” ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["1"],"id":"fnref1","href":"#fn1"}]},"), which Network Upgrade 7 deploys instead. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["2"],"id":"fnref2","href":"#fn2"}]}]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Terminology"],"id":"terminology"},{"tag":"p","children":["The key word “MUST” in this document is to be interpreted as described in BCP 14 ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["3"],"id":"fnref3","href":"#fn3"}]}," when, and only when, it appears in all capitals."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The term “network upgrade” in this document is to be interpreted as described in ZIP 200. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["4"],"id":"fnref4","href":"#fn4"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The character § is used when referring to sections of the Zcash Protocol Specification. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["5"],"id":"fnref5","href":"#fn5"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The terms “Mainnet” and “Testnet” are to be interpreted as described in § 3.12 ‘Mainnet and Testnet’. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["6"],"id":"fnref6","href":"#fn6"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The symbol “",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mspace","children":[],"attrs":{"width":"0.1667em"}},{"tag":"mo","children":["⋅"]},{"tag":"mspace","children":[],"attrs":{"width":"0.1667em"}}]},"” means multiplication, as described in § 2 ‘Notation’. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["7"],"id":"fnref7","href":"#fn7"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["“ZEC/TAZ” refers to the native currency of Zcash on a given network, i.e. ZEC on Mainnet and TAZ on Testnet."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The terms “Block Subsidy” and “Issuance” are to be interpreted as described in ZIP 233. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["8"],"id":"fnref8","href":"#fn8"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["Let ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖯"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖡"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗅"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗈"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗆"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖧"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗅"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗏"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗀"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖨"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗇"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗋"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗏"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖺"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗅"]}]}]}," be as defined in ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["9"],"id":"fnref9","href":"#fn9"}]},"."]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖷"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖤"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖸"]}]}]},", as defined in § 5.3 ‘Constants’ ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["10"],"id":"fnref10","href":"#fn10"}]},", is the total ZEC/TAZ supply cap measured in zatoshi, corresponding to 21,000,000 ZEC. This is slightly larger than the supply cap for the current issuance mechanism, but is the value used in existing critical consensus checks."]},{"tag":"p","children":["“Issued Supply” - The Issued Supply at a given height of a block chain is the total ZEC/TAZ value in all chain value pool balances at that height, as calculated by ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖨"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖽"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗉"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗉"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗅"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗒"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["("],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}},{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗁"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗀"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗁"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":[")"],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}}]}," defined in § 4.17 ‘Chain Value Pool Balances’. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["11"],"id":"fnref11","href":"#fn11"}]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["“Money Reserve” - The Money Reserve at a given height of a block chain is the total ZEC/TAZ value remaining to be issued, as calculated by ",{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖷"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖬"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖤"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖸"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["−"]},{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖨"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗌"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖽"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗎"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗉"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗉"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗅"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗒"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["("],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}},{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗁"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖾"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗂"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗀"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗁"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝗍"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":[")"],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}}]},"."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Abstract"],"id":"abstract"},{"tag":"p","children":["This ZIP proposes a change to how nodes calculate the block subsidy."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Instead of following a step function around the 4-year halving intervals inherited from Bitcoin, we propose a smooth logarithmic curve, defined as a fixed portion of the current value of the Money Reserve at a given block height."]},{"tag":"p","children":["The new issuance scheme would approximate the current issuance over 4-year intervals, assuming no ZEC/TAZ is removed from circulation during that time, and retains the overall supply cap of ",{"tag":"code","children":["MAX_MONEY"]},"."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Motivation"],"id":"motivation"},{"tag":"p","children":["The current block reward halving schedule is fixed and does not provide a way to “recycle” funds removed from circulation via ZIP-233 into future issuance. Once scheduled issuance ends, the network becomes reliant on transaction fees for the security budget."]},{"tag":"p","children":["Key Objectives:"]},{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["We want to introduce an automated mechanism that allows users of the network to contribute to the long-term sustainability of the network."]},{"tag":"li","children":["We want to enable ZEC that has been removed from circulation to be reissued in the future to benefit network sustainability."]},{"tag":"li","children":["We want to retain the existing ZEC supply cap of 21 million."]},{"tag":"li","children":["We want the issuance rate to remain similar to the historical rate for Zcash (and before that, Bitcoin)."]},{"tag":"li","children":["We want issuance to be easy for all network users to understand and predict."]},{"tag":"li","children":["We want the new issuance to activate at a block with as minimal a delta from the current issuance as possible."]}]},{"tag":"p","children":["The current Zcash economic model, inherited from Bitcoin, includes a halving mechanism that dictates the issuance of new coins via the mining block reward. Halvings have since become culturally foundational, but abrupt reductions in miner revenue can lead to short-term drops in mining participation, as evidenced by hashrate/difficulty."]},{"tag":"p","children":["In Zcash, difficulty declined materially after recent halving events: following the 2020-11-18 halving, weekly difficulty fell about 20.6% within roughly a week and was still about 9.1% lower around 30 days later. Following the 2024-11-23 halving, weekly difficulty fell about 17% within roughly a week and about 23% around 30 days later. ",{"tag":"sup","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["12"],"id":"fnref12","href":"#fn12"}]}," As difficulty adjusts in response to hashrate, these short-term drops are consistent with discrete subsidy cuts producing measurable reductions in mining participation."]},{"tag":"p","children":["While Bitcoin halvings are often accompanied by bullish narratives and have sometimes been followed by strong price performance, Zcash has not consistently followed the same pattern. Thus, by smoothing out the issuance curve, we mitigate the risks associated with abrupt changes in issuance rates."]},{"tag":"p","children":["This new NSM-based issuance scheme addresses these problems by ensuring a more consistent and predictable rate of coin issuance, while preserving the core aspects of Zcash’s issuance policy and the 21-million-coin cap. Critically, it establishes the intended path for ZEC that has been voluntarily removed from circulation, as well as transaction fees that are deliberately redirected into the reserve: these funds are automatically and algorithmically reissued over future block subsidies, ensuring they benefit the network’s long-term security."]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Requirements"],"id":"requirements"},{"tag":"p","children":["Smoothing the issuance curve is possible using an exponential decay formula that satisfies the following requirements:"]},{"tag":"ol","children":[{"tag":"li","children":["The issuance can be summarized into a reasonably simple explanation."]},{"tag":"li","children":["Block subsidies approximate a continuous function."]},{"tag":"li","children":["If the Money Reserve is greater than 0, then the block subsidy must be non-zero, preventing any final “unmined” zatoshis."]},{"tag":"li","children":["For any 4-year period, all paid out block subsidies are approximately equal to half of the Money Reserve at the beginning of that 4-year period, if no ZEC is removed from circulation during those 4 years."]},{"tag":"li","children":["Decrease the short-term impact of the deployment of this ZIP on block subsidy recipients, and minimize the potential reputation risk to Zcash of changing the block subsidy amount."]},{"tag":"li","children":["The immediate change in issuance when this mechanism activates should be minimal."]}]},{"tag":"h2","children":["Specification"],"id":"specification"},{"tag":"h3","children":["Parameters"],"id":"parameters"},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"math","children":[{"tag":"mrow","children":[{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖡"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖫"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖢"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖪"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖴"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖡"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖲"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖨"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖣"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖸"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖥"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖱"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖠"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖢"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖳"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖨"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖮"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["𝖭"]}]},{"tag":"mo","children":["="]},{"tag":"mn","children":["4126"]},{"tag":"mo","children":["/"],"attrs":{"stretchy":"false"}},{"tag":"mn","children":["10"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["000"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["000"]},{"tag":"mi","children":["_"]},{"tag":"mn","children":["000"]},{"tag":"mo","children":["="]},{"tag":"mn","children":["0.0000004126"]